<title>MEXICO: Banco de Mexico to drain 1.594 bln pesos.</title>
<headline>Banco de Mexico to drain 1.594 bln pesos.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-06-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Banco de Mexico sought to drain 1.594 billion pesos from the secondary market on Friday through three direct sales and three repurchasing agreements, dealers said.</p>
<p>The three direct sales were as follows:</p>
<p>    AMOUNT     TERM		RATE</p>
<p>    150 million    342 days	  21.65</p>
<p>    150 million    180 days	  n/a</p>
<p>    150 million     90 days	  n/a</p>
<p>The three repurchase agreements were as follows:</p>
<p>    AMOUNT     TERM</p>
<p>    400 million    34 days</p>
<p>    500 million    25 days</p>
<p>    244 million     3 days</p>
<p>*Amounts in pesos</p>
<p>((--Mexico City newsroom +525 728-9559))</p>
</text>
